cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PyTestLab: Scientific test and measurement automation for Python"
message: "If you use PyTestLab in scientific work, please cite this software."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Olowe
    given-names: Emmanuel A.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3172-1948"
  - family-names: Chitnis
    given-names: Danial
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-06-18"
repository-code: "https://github.com/labiium/pytestlab"
url: "https://pytestlab.org"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  PyTestLab is a Python toolbox for laboratory test-and-measurement automation,
  uncertainty-aware waveform analysis, deterministic simulation/replay, and
  software-validation evidence generation. PyTestLab evidence artifacts are not
  accreditation certificates and do not confer ISO/IEC 17025 accreditation.
keywords:
  - test-and-measurement
  - metrology
  - uncertainty
  - oscilloscope
  - laboratory-automation
